  "description": "The paint-to-stain change story chg-1 is approved on Friday. A Tuesday A-601 issuance that already shows stain is entered on Saturday, so Thursday's revision changes no property. Maintenance records the reconstructed reconciliation with an empty @transitions and the related change story chg-1+1 (paint to stain on Tuesday); it revises chg-1's begin act to null (chg-1/v1) and revises its review end act (chg-1/v2) to cause reconstructed, with the backfilled Assertion as record and at null. The approval stays as recorded and chg-1 still reads reviewed, but its ending is reconstructed, at every cutoff, with no period. Withdrawing the approval returns chg-1 to unreviewed and begins no period, so it is never open or pending again; only chg-1+1 awaits review.",
  "note": "Step 6: 7.6.10: \"A period's ending under a policy gets a new end act when its begin act has none for that policy; otherwise the existing end act is revised\"; chg-1/b1 already has the review end act chg-1/e1, so 7.6.12's one baseline end act (\"for backfilled evidence, cause `reconstructed`, with the backfilled Assertion as its record and `at` `null`\") is that act, revised. Step 15: 7.6.2: \"A change story whose revision a correction or backfilled evidence (7.3.7) leaves changing no property has no period (7.2.7, 7.6.12)\", and 7.6.12: reads \"report the story as ended at every cutoff\", so the withdrawal records no begin act; the review dimension follows 9.5.2.",
